  "tip": [
    {
      "id": "p1",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "t": "strong",
          "v": "注意"
        },
        {
          "t": "text",
          "v": " 在现代英语中 except 和 except for 有混用的趋势，尤其在含有 all、none、no 等词的句中。"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "p2",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "t": "text",
          "v": "He answered all the questions "
        },
        {
          "t": "underline",
          "v": "except (for)"
        },
        {
          "t": "text",
          "v": " the last one. 除最后一个问题外，他回答了所有问题。"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "compare": [
    {
      "words": "except, except for",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "id": "c1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "t": "strong",
              "v": "except"
            },
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": " 用于同类事物的排除，不能置于句首，可接从句。"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "c2",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": "He gets up early every day "
            },
            {
              "t": "underline",
              "v": "except"
            },
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": " Sunday. 除了星期天，他每天起得很早。"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "c3",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": "I know nothing about him "
            },
            {
              "t": "underline",
              "v": "except"
            },
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": " that he is from Britain. 除了知道他从英国来，其他有关他的情况我一无所知。"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "c4",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "t": "strong",
              "v": "except for"
            },
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": " 用于异类事物的排除，可置于句首。"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "c5",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": "The garden was silent "
            },
            {
              "t": "underline",
              "v": "except for"
            },
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": " the leaves. 除了叶子的沙沙声，这个花园寂静无声。"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "c6",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "t": "underline",
              "v": "Except for"
            },
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": " Sam, you can all go home. 除了萨姆，你们都能回家。"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
